00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:04.420
JOE: There are a range of different
initiatives, organisations and agencies

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:09.370
and companies that can help individuals
with autism into employment and some also

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:13.739
offer employment directly focusing on the
skills individuals with autism can offer.

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:17.959
BETH: 'The National Autistic Society'
provides resources and a variety of

00:00:17.959 --> 00:00:22.720
work programmes, training and resources
for jobseekers with autism and can

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:27.090
help employers looking to benefit
from hiring a more diverse workforce.

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:31.279
JOE: ‘Ambitious about Autism’
is a national charity that has a

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:35.099
website covering a range of things
including getting into employment.

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:39.350
They run employability programmes
acting as a bridge to employment for

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:41.800
autistic people by removing barriers.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:45.699
They work with employers giving them
access to talented and innovative

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:49.829
autistic employees and promote paid
work experience for individuals.

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:52.810
They also provide training
resources and mentorship.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:57.340
BETH: ‘Auticon’ is an international
information technology consulting

00:00:57.340 --> 00:01:00.990
firm company that exclusively
hires individuals with autism.

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:05.239
It employs their cognitive
diversity and specific talents to

00:01:05.239 --> 00:01:09.189
supply services for many blue-chip
organisations throughout the world.

00:01:09.849 --> 00:01:14.600
It embraces the extraordinary abilities
that individuals with autism can have and

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:16.600
their unique approach to problem solving.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:20.770
JOE: The way individuals with high
functioning autism think can make

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:24.690
them more valued in the workplace,
and as companies can see the

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:28.799
opportunities to employ neuro-diverse
individuals, then this may help

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:30.569
others on the autistic spectrum.

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:35.110
BETH: Neuro-diverse people are wired
differently and can bring new perspectives

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:38.969
to a company and can make up for
the skills shortages in technology

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:41.330
companies and other digital industries.

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:45.120
JOE: More companies are looking to
recruit individuals who offer technical

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:49.589
talents and have attention to detail
and systematic approaches to tasks.

00:01:49.589 --> 00:01:54.960
In a world that relies more on digital
development this can only expand further.
